!Name: grow-t13
!C Population is asymptotic to  C t^(1/3),  where  C = (75/16)^(1/3).
!C In particular, in gen  720 n3 + 28620 n2 + 60n + 3840
!C the population is  15n + 4524.
!C This uses two salvos which are sent toward blocks along the
!C southeast diagonal.  Usually there are 2 blocks on the diagonal.
!C At such times, a 3-glider salvo pulls the nearest block 5 units
!C and sends back a glider.  This is done repeatedly, waiting for the
!C return glider from each pull before sending the next one.  When the
!C nearest block is pulled as far back as possible, it is deleted, and
!C a 5-glider salvo is sent toward the other block; the salvo
!C duplicates the block, creating a new one 10 units farther away and
!C another one 10 units closer.
!C Deleting the eater on the western edge of the pattern gives
!C population asymptotic to  C2 t^(2/3),  where  C2 = (45/256)^(1/3).
!C In particular, in gen  720 n3 + 28620 n2 + 60 n + 3840
!C the population is  45 n2 + 15n + 4522.
!C Dean Hickerson, 10/10/2006
!
